<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Draupadi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Draupadi is the heroine of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> epic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>, daughter of King Drupada of Panchala and the common wife of the five Pandava brothers. Her humiliation in the Kaurava court, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yudhishthira">Yudhishthira</a> lost her in a game of dice, is one of the epic's central episodes and a cause of the great war at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurukshetra">Kurukshetra</a>. She is venerated as a goddess in parts of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/draupadi.jpg" alt="Draupadi" width="320" height="569" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raja Ravi Varma · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Draupadi,_Raja_Ravi_Varma.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
